1
00:00:08,849 --> 00:00:13,002
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُم
وَالصَّلاةُ وَالسَّلامُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللهِ وَعَلَى آلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ اَجْمَعِينَ
ثُمَّ اَمَّا بَعْدُ

2
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:23,370
Some people ask this question: Why does Allah use "We" in the Qur'an?  I will address this because it has to do with the literary analysis of the Qur'an.

3
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:25,190
I'll give you some good notes on that bi-iznillah.

4
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:29,000
Hopefully that will help you understand an overview of the subject.

5
00:00:29,010 --> 00:00:31,720
Let's answer this step by step,

6
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,530
let's take a methodical approach to answering this question.

7
00:00:34,530 --> 00:00:35,550
The first thing is

8
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:37,190
the pronouns

9
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:41,760
used for Allah are: I

10
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:43,760
We

11
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:45,360
You

12
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:47,050
and He.

13
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:51,800
Meaning in the Qur'an Allah uses "I" for Himself, "We" for Himself, "You" for Himself.

14
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:54,871
and He for Himself. For example, when We make Du"a to Allah

15
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:56,320
We use what word? You.

16
00:00:56,344 --> 00:00:58,707
أَنتَ مَوْلَىٰنَا فَٱنصُرْنَا عَلَى ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ

17
00:00:58,746 --> 00:01:03,251
(أَنتَ) You. Okay? Allah says I for Himself, like
وَأَنَا التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ

18
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:04,959
I am the one who accepts Tawbah.

19
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:08,232
We use the word Who or He as in

20
00:01:08,256 --> 00:01:10,256
قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ

21
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:12,140
We use the word "We" as in

22
00:01:12,164 --> 00:01:13,526
إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا الذِّكْرَ

23
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:18,150
We are the ones Who sent down the remembrance. So all four of these pronouns are used.

24
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:21,320
Now if you know at least third grade level english,

25
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:25,160
you know that "I" and "we" are first person, "you" is second person and "he" is

26
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:26,790
third person. Yes.

27
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:31,820
You also know if you know the basics that "I" is singular, "we" is plural,

28
00:01:31,830 --> 00:01:33,960
"you" is singular and "he" is also

29
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:36,220
singular. Now, what were they-

30
00:01:36,230 --> 00:01:41,400
what we're saying then is that in the first person you find singular and plural.

31
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:42,160
Isn't that true?

32
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:46,260
You find singular and plural? But in the second person you only find

33
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:47,300
singular.

34
00:01:47,460 --> 00:01:49,850
And in the third person, you also only find

35
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:50,860
singular.

36
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:55,560
This is important to note because if the plural was literally plural,

37
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,750
then you would find the plural in the first person.

38
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,540
You would find the plural in the second person.

39
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:04,820
And you would also find the plural in the third person. In other words,

40
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,480
you would also find instead of "you", you would find "you all"

41
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:12,060
and instead of "he" (هو), you would also find "they" (هم).

42
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:16,840
But you don't. You don't consistently find the plural in all the persons.

43
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:19,150
You only find it in first person and even

44
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:22,250
within first person you find both singular and plural.

45
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:23,260
Is that clear to everybody?

46
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:24,170
Okay.

47
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:26,560
So now what we're trying to say then is that the

48
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:31,010
use of "We" in the Qur'an for Allah is not consistent.

49
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,690
Therefore it is not literal.

50
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:37,290
The first observation is: it is not consistent because if it was consistent

51
00:02:37,290 --> 00:02:42,260
it would have been "I" and "we" and "you" and "you all" and "he" and

52
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:45,590
"they". All of that would have been there. None of that is there.

53
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,460
Okay then the second issue,

54
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:53,700
if you think of the third-- we can take "you" out of the picture here.

55
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:57,350
We can take "you" out of the picture. Why can we take "you" out of the picture?

56
00:02:57,350 --> 00:03:01,310
Because "you" is only used when there's a Du'a. When we are talking to Allah,

57
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:04,750
we are saying You forgive us or You help us or You something.

58
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:08,360
We're talking to Him. But really when Allah is speaking on His own behalf

59
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:10,060
then you find these three

60
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:12,130
"I" and "We" and "He".

61
00:03:12,390 --> 00:03:15,250
Those are the three you find when Allah speaks on His own behalf.

62
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:17,470
Now, speaking of these three,

63
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:20,090
what is the difference between first person and third person?

64
00:03:20,090 --> 00:03:23,260
All of you know, first person is when you speak on your own behalf.

65
00:03:23,270 --> 00:03:25,860
Third person is when you're speaking about someone else.

66
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:30,890
But rhetorically speaking in the literary sense, there's another difference.

67
00:03:31,130 --> 00:03:33,160
The "I" and the "We" is close

68
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,350
and the "he" is far away.

69
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:39,560
The "he" is far away. Third person is someone who is away from you.

70
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:43,690
This raises an issue in the Qur'an,

71
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:47,262
a literary observation that Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala

72
00:03:47,350 --> 00:03:49,560
in the Qur'an sometimes uses the word "He"

73
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:52,950
for Himself, even though He's the One speaking.

74
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,980
He's the One-- when you're speaking about yourself, do you use "he"?

75
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:02,100
Unless you're a politician named Bob Dole from the 90's.

76
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:06,000
Bob Dole is not a liar. He's a reliable man.

77
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,760
You're right there dude.

78
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:14,390
Okay, so sometimes people use he for themselves. That's kind of crazy.

79
00:04:14,410 --> 00:04:17,050
But normally when people speak, what do they use for themselves?

80
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:19,430
"I". They use "I" for themselves.

81
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:22,570
So it raises a strange question; if Allah's the speaker in the Qur'an

82
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,560
how come He's using the word He anyway?

83
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:27,260
How come He's even using the word "Allah"?

84
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:30,410
This is the difference between a speaker and a teacher.

85
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:34,220
The Qur'an was not-- is not an autobiography of God.

86
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:36,900
It is not Allah speaking for His own sake.

87
00:04:36,910 --> 00:04:39,340
It is actually Allah speaking for our sake.

88
00:04:39,350 --> 00:04:41,460
In other words Allah has given us a curriculum.

89
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:44,850
Now, let me tell you the practical benefits of that.

90
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:46,250
Practically speaking

91
00:04:46,390 --> 00:04:50,550
like Allah does not say, 'I am forgiving.' He says 'Allah is forgiving.'

92
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:53,785
Right? So the words of Allah
وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ

93
00:04:54,110 --> 00:04:58,760
And I'll just say it in simple
english. Allah is extremely forgiving.

94
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:01,360
Let's just say.

95
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:05,960
As opposed to saying 'I am extremely forgiving.'

96
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:10,360
Now let me give you a scenario. You're talking to your friend,

97
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:13,740
you're having a conversation with your friend and your friend is losing hope.

98
00:05:13,750 --> 00:05:15,150
They think that Allah will punish them

99
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,680
and you want to give them hope.

100
00:05:18,010 --> 00:05:20,380
And you want to give them hope from Allah's word Itself.

101
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:23,630
So you put your arm around their shoulder and you

102
00:05:23,630 --> 00:05:28,460
remind them what Allah says, when Allah says
وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ
Allah is forgiving.

103
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:32,780
It would be really awkward if Allah revealed in the Qur'an,

104
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:36,200
'I am extremely forgiving' and you put your arm around your friend's shoulder and say,

105
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:39,510
'Hey listen relax, (انا غفور رحيم).'

106
00:05:41,940 --> 00:05:43,350
'I am extremely forgiving.'

107
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:45,360
You understand?

108
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:47,480
In other words

109
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:50,540
Allah revealed the Qur'an in a way that makes it

110
00:05:50,550 --> 00:05:55,440
easy for me to use it to remind
myself and remind others.

111
00:05:55,750 --> 00:06:00,142
And there's another meaning of
وَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا ٱلْقُرْءَانَ لِلذِّكْرِ

112
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:04,500
He facilitated the language in a way that when you

113
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:07,350
remind someone else, they can actually get what you're saying.

114
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,660
The language is structured in that way.

115
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:10,960
But even then

116
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:13,370
I want you to note some things.

117
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:15,150
The word "he",

118
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:20,550
the word "he" illustrate-- is formal.

119
00:06:21,626 --> 00:06:23,760
Is formal.

120
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,450
It can even be distant.

121
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,880
It can even be distant.

122
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:34,160
In other words, sometimes Allah is talking to someone directly.

123
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,560
And He's upset with them.

124
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:41,995
And immediately He switches over and instead
of talking to them, He says
واللهُ

125
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:44,760
'And Allah is' and so on and so forth. He distanced Himself.

126
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:47,550
That can happen. It's called the concept of (التبعيد).

127
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,160
التبعيد-- distancing oneself. Okay.

128
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:54,450
The word "We"- or let's use "We" at the end- "I"

129
00:06:56,010 --> 00:06:57,480
is used in intense

130
00:06:58,940 --> 00:06:59,960
contexts.

131
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:03,160
Extreme love.

132
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,260
Or extreme anger.

133
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:10,890
When you find the word "I" in the Qur'an,

134
00:07:11,740 --> 00:07:13,360
then it can only be extremes.

135
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,110
It is not a normal thing,

136
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:16,560
it's just not.

137
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:21,760
And it's powerful because you know, kings of old times,

138
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,920
they used to speak of themselves in the plural

139
00:07:24,230 --> 00:07:26,560
'We have spoken', 'We have declared'

140
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:29,430
'This is our land', etcetera, etcetera.

141
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:33,250
But when the king got really angry, he said, 'You dare speak to me like that?'

142
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:38,660
He doesn't say 'You dare speak to us', he says, 'You dare speak to me.'

143
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:40,860
'Who do you think I am?'

144
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:46,060
Not "We are". When he gets
extremely angry, he uses I.

145
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:48,060
He likes somebody he goes, 'I like you.'

146
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:53,030
It's not, 'We like you'. He just says, 'I like you' because it becomes informal.

147
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,060
It becomes intimate.

148
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:56,541
So the the use of "I" in the Qur'an

149
00:07:56,620 --> 00:08:00,610
is either extreme love or extreme anger. I'll give you one example of each.

150
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:02,450
So you have some idea what I'm talking about.

151
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,950
Forgiveness is awesome.

152
00:08:04,950 --> 00:08:09,216
But even greater than forgiveness is the act of Tawbah from Allah.

153
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:12,200
There's two kinds of Tawbah: Tawbah of the human being and

154
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:13,240
Tawbah of Allah.

155
00:08:13,510 --> 00:08:16,680
Tawbah of the human being means the human being turned back to Allah.

156
00:08:16,705 --> 00:08:22,190
Tawbah of Allah is that Allah turned back to the human being. Which is why the word (التواب)

157
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:23,660
is a name of Allah.

158
00:08:24,150 --> 00:08:26,510
And (التواب) is also used for human beings.

159
00:08:26,730 --> 00:08:29,844
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ التَّوَّابِينَ

160
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:33,289
Because in the sense of Allah, Allah is turning back

161
00:08:33,289 --> 00:08:35,909
to the human being and the sense of the human being,

162
00:08:35,909 --> 00:08:37,618
he's turning back to Allah.

163
00:08:37,682 --> 00:08:40,150
But I want to share something about the word Tawbah

164
00:08:40,179 --> 00:08:44,020
with you. Imagine a human being that has done a lot of bad things,

165
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:47,580
they've done a lot of lying, a lot of cheating, a lot of really bad, horrible,

166
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:48,450
horrible things.

167
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:51,280
They haven't prayed, they haven't done any good thing in their life,

168
00:08:51,290 --> 00:08:55,340
etcetera. And eventually they decide one day something happens in their

169
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:57,450
heart and they decide that they're going to do Tawbah,

170
00:08:57,630 --> 00:09:01,110
they're going to turn back to Allah and they're going to start fresh.

171
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:03,920
But the problem is even though this guy wants to get a new start,

172
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,950
he's got a pretty big criminal record,

173
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:09,260
he's got a mountain size of evil deeds.

174
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:12,370
Allah offers people who make Tawbah

175
00:09:12,394 --> 00:09:16,165
فَأُولَئِكَ يُبَدِّلُ اللَّهُ سَيِّئَاتِهِمْ حَسَنَاتٍ

176
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:18,940
People who make Tawbah to Allah,

177
00:09:18,940 --> 00:09:22,660
those people Allah will replace their mountain of evil deeds

178
00:09:22,763 --> 00:09:25,590
convert it into a mountain of good deeds.

179
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:29,160
Now, this is different from forgiveness.

180
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:34,190
Because when you talk about forgiveness, that means 'I will erase your bad deeds.'

181
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:37,030
That is, 'I will erase your bad deeds.'

182
00:09:37,230 --> 00:09:41,440
But when you talk about Tawbah then Allah is saying, I won't just erase your bad deeds

183
00:09:41,590 --> 00:09:44,060
I will convert your bad deeds into what?

184
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:49,190
Good deeds. Those bad deeds were going to be the reason for you to burn in hell.

185
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:52,320
Now that you have made Tawbah those same bad deeds have actually been

186
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:57,070
converted into something that counts in your favor simply because you made Tawbah.

187
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:59,590
This is far greater than the act of forgiveness.

188
00:09:59,590 --> 00:10:02,350
This is actually- you're being rewarded

189
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:06,390
And your crimes that were held against you- imagine you have debt.

190
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:11,060
Just imagine this scenario, you have debt. You owe someone 20,000 ringets.

191
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:16,960
And all of a sudden you check your bank account and instead of minus-20,000 it says what?

192
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:21,350
Not even zero. Even if it's a zero, you should be really happy.

193
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:24,560
It doesn't say zero, it says you just made 20,000.

194
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,460
That's crazy.

195
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:32,350
So, that unusual act of Allah's love, you will find (انا) associated with Tawbah.

196
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:34,228
أَنَا التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ

197
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:39,750
'I am extremely forgiving, extremely accepting of repentance.'

198
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,160
When I turned back to you, I really turned back to you.

199
00:10:43,940 --> 00:10:46,630
That's the idea. That is an example of extreme love.

200
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:49,860
What about an example of extreme what? Anger.

201
00:10:51,092 --> 00:10:55,590
'Isa 'alaihissalam, Jesus, is the last messenger sent to the Israelites.

202
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:59,160
The Israelites have a long history of prophets. Yes or no?

203
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:03,090
And these prophets were given many, many, many miracles.

204
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:07,160
Starting with Moses, starting with Musa 'alaihissalam, they were given the staff,

205
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:10,620
they were given the water parting, they were given the clouds following them.

206
00:11:10,630 --> 00:11:14,010
Then they were given, you know, 'Uzair 'alaihissalam

207
00:11:14,010 --> 00:11:17,200
who died for 100 years and was brought back to life.

208
00:11:17,210 --> 00:11:21,180
They were given Sulaiman 'alaihissalam and Dawud 'alaihissalam.

209
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:23,730
They were given prophet after prophet after prophet.

210
00:11:23,730 --> 00:11:26,060
Miracle after miracle after miracle.

211
00:11:26,070 --> 00:11:30,180
They have an exhaustive history of remarkable gifts from Allah.

212
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:32,020
The final prophet that comes to them.

213
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:35,130
The final messenger that comes to them is Jesus, is 'Isa 'alaihissalam.

214
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:39,583
And he has very few followers. They're called the Hawariyun (حواريون).

215
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:43,252
And they're-- he's sitting with his Hawariyun (حواريون).

216
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:46,579
And these followers of his they asked him,

217
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,460
'Hey, could you make Du'a to Allah?'

218
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:56,460
'He could send us a meal. A full table's worth meal from the sky.'

219
00:11:59,140 --> 00:12:00,460
It's called the last supper.

220
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:02,260
Right?

221
00:12:02,940 --> 00:12:05,040
Could you send us a meal from the sky?

222
00:12:08,233 --> 00:12:12,030
'Isa 'alaihissalam hears these words and he says,

223
00:12:12,054 --> 00:12:12,666
اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ

224
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:14,060
'What is wrong with you people?

225
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,760
Why are you asking me for this?'

226
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:21,360
They say, 'Because if we see this miracle, it will confirm our faith.'

227
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,610
Because the believer sometimes wants to see

228
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:25,270
a miracle and they've seen previous ones,

229
00:12:25,270 --> 00:12:28,190
but they just want to see this one and obviously they want to see this one to

230
00:12:28,190 --> 00:12:29,930
settle their hearts because they're about to be killed

231
00:12:29,930 --> 00:12:32,320
by the romans or there's an extreme situation.

232
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,810
So they're they're looking for something to ease their hearts.

233
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:36,650
So they asked for it, fine.

234
00:12:37,704 --> 00:12:38,750
'Isa 'alaihissalam

235
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:39,790
you know,

236
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:43,880
asks Allah for this table spread, for this ma'idah (مائدة) from the sky.

237
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:46,440
And Allah responds. And Allah says, 'I will send it to you.'

238
00:12:46,450 --> 00:12:46,850
Fine.

239
00:12:47,450 --> 00:12:48,260
I will give it to you.

240
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:49,460
But

241
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:54,260
if anyone of you disbelieves after this one.

242
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:59,500
Now Allah is talking to the last messenger of the Israelites

243
00:12:59,940 --> 00:13:08,180
Who after all the disbelief and all the hypocrisy are still asking for one last miracle.

244
00:13:09,130 --> 00:13:12,660
Allah says, if if anybody dares to disbelieve after this one,

245
00:13:12,884 --> 00:13:17,612
فَإِنِّىٓ أُعَذِّبُهُۥ عَذَابًا لَّآ أُعَذِّبُهُۥٓ أَحَدًا مِّنَ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ

246
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:19,320
'Then no doubt about it

247
00:13:19,330 --> 00:13:23,140
I, I am going to torture him with a torture

248
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:27,750
that I have never tortured anyone of any nation ever.'

249
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:31,440
There's a lot of "I" in that Ayah.

250
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:36,360
And it's not a normal Ayah. It's an Ayah expressing Allah's extreme what?

251
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:37,660
Anger.

252
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:42,920
So the "I" is used for extreme love or extreme anger. You with me so far?

253
00:13:42,930 --> 00:13:44,560
Now we come to the money question.

254
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:46,250
When is "We" used?

255
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:50,600
"We" is used when Allah describes

256
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:53,260
something that is associated with Allah's kingdom.

257
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:56,300
Because kings used to use "We".

258
00:13:56,490 --> 00:13:57,950
That's the first usage of "We".

259
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:03,370
Which is why you will find unusually in the Qur'an overwhelmingly when water is mentioned,

260
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:04,750
"We" is mentioned.

261
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:09,460
It will be-- the rest of the Ayah will be "He", "He", "He", "He", "He" and then

262
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:13,760
water comes up and it becomes "We". 'And We gave water' and 'We grew the earth.'

263
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:18,070
So the Kingdom of Allah and water and things that are associated with water.

264
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:21,060
You will find "We" overwhelmingly.

265
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:26,160
This is also interesting because the throne of Allah, His 'Arsh is on what?

266
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:30,760
Water. The water itself is associated with the Kingdom of Allah 'azzawajal.

267
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:32,930
It's a manifestation of His Kingdom.

268
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:37,650
And water is a means by which not only is water pure it is also a purifier.

269
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:38,860
Right?

270
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:42,640
And in the physical sense it's pure and it's a physical purifier.

271
00:14:42,650 --> 00:14:46,860
And in the spiritual sense it cleanses us so we can pray. You make Wudu using water.

272
00:14:47,640 --> 00:14:48,060
Okay.

273
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:53,660
So with water you find manifestation of Allah's kingdom.

274
00:14:53,685 --> 00:14:56,320
When Allah gives unusual gifts.

275
00:14:57,940 --> 00:15:01,340
So kings give-- and by the way, including within kingdom

276
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,350
there's water,

277
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:04,750
there's gifts, there's life.

278
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:09,060
You know, major things Allah will use "We".

279
00:15:10,020 --> 00:15:11,270
Allah will use "We".

280
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:15,050
So "He" is for formality, "We" is for

281
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:19,340
big gifts, of grand gifts of Allah, grand accomplishments.

282
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:24,060
But that's still, you know, it leaves something to be wondered.

283
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:29,450
What I find really most amazing about the use of "We" in the Qur'an

284
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:32,060
is that Allah did not leave us in confusion.

285
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:38,320
Every single time Allah uses "We" for Himself in the Qur'an

286
00:15:38,330 --> 00:15:40,150
it is immediately followed

287
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:44,260
by use of the word-- of the singular for Allah.

288
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:50,070
Something immediately follows up just to let you know, by the way, don't be confused.

289
00:15:50,070 --> 00:15:50,760
He's still one.

290
00:15:51,410 --> 00:15:53,050
The "We" is just being used for grandeur.

291
00:15:53,740 --> 00:15:55,220
I'll give you an easy example of that.

292
00:15:55,490 --> 00:15:57,105
إِنَّا أَعْطَيْنَاكَ الْكَوْثَرَ

293
00:15:57,130 --> 00:15:58,150
Everybody knows that one.

294
00:15:58,940 --> 00:16:00,455
We gave you Kauthar.

295
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:01,850
So which word is being used?

296
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:02,750
"We".

297
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:04,560
What's the next Ayah?

298
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:09,360
فَصَلِّ لِرَبِّكَ وَانْحَرْ
not (فصل لنا وانحر)

299
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:15,650
See We gave you Kauthar so pray to us. That's the expectation. We gave

300
00:16:15,650 --> 00:16:21,870
you Kauthar pray to us and sacrifice. No, He says We gave you Kauthar, pray to your Master.

301
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:23,160
How many masters?

302
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:24,980
One Master and sacrifice.

303
00:16:25,910 --> 00:16:29,650
Immediately after "We" the word Rabb, which is singular.

304
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:32,550
Over and over again in the Qur'an.

305
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:35,890
There will be a "We" immediately followed

306
00:16:35,890 --> 00:16:38,760
by something specifically singular for Allah.

307
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:41,660
Specifically singular for Allah.

308
00:16:42,830 --> 00:16:44,660
إِنَّا أَنزَلْنَاهُ فِي لَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ

309
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:47,360
We sent it down in the night of power.

310
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,670
Then the conversations about Laylatul Qadr.

311
00:16:52,321 --> 00:16:54,959
لَيْلَةُ الْقَدْرِ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ أَلْفِ شَهْرٍ

312
00:16:54,983 --> 00:16:59,305
تَنَزَّلُ الْمَلائِكَةُ وَالرُّوحُ فِيهَا

313
00:16:59,330 --> 00:17:00,230
(بِإِذْنِنا)?

314
00:17:02,210 --> 00:17:03,801
(بِإِذْنِ)?

315
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:05,119
( رَبِّ) Rabb-singular.

316
00:17:05,143 --> 00:17:07,143
بهِم مِّن كُلِّ أَمْرٍ

317
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,460
Immediately Rabb again.

318
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:14,859
In other words Allah does not let us remain in the plural "We" ever.

319
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,460
He switches over to the singular every time.

320
00:17:18,339 --> 00:17:23,040
I asked Jewish scholar one time, a rabbi that I met, does God use "We"

321
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:27,079
for Himself in the Torah, in the Hebrew Torah that you guys have? He goes, 'Yeah.'

322
00:17:27,089 --> 00:17:27,960
'Of course all the time.'

323
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:32,270
I was like, 'Really? So do you think that God is many?' He goes, 'No, that's stupid.'

324
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:34,210
'He's one.'

325
00:17:34,390 --> 00:17:36,670
'"We" is used because He's majestic. He's a king.'

326
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:39,670
I was like, 'Okay, so you guys have always been clear.'

327
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:43,960
They have been clear all along. It's not like they'e confused about it.

328
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:48,140
And then in the middle came the Christians who somehow

329
00:17:48,140 --> 00:17:50,660
got confused about this and then it comes to us.

330
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:52,660
You know, finally.

331
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:56,760
But we shouldn't be confused about this matter. Is that-- is that clear to everybody?

332
00:17:56,770 --> 00:17:59,460
This was a side note. I want to get to the examples I really want to get to.

333
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:03,770
Oh this is.

334
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:05,860
Oh man.

335
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:16,460
I wrote some important things down. I want to make sure I don't miss them.

336
00:18:20,340 --> 00:18:20,760
Okay.

337
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:34,100
People an example is about to be given. Please listen to it carefully.

338
00:18:34,870 --> 00:18:37,110
Who listened to the example carefully in

339
00:18:37,134 --> 00:18:40,043
إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ لَن يَخْلُقُواْ ذُبَابًا

340
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:41,290
No doubt about it.

341
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:46,680
Those who you call other than Allah will not be able to create a single fly.

342
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:50,360
Those who you are trying to call other than Allah

343
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:52,660
will not be able to create a single fly.

344
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:55,408
Now (إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ)

345
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:58,615
does not say (إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَهم مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ)

346
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,245
This is called the concept of 'Ai'd.

347
00:19:00,270 --> 00:19:02,420
No technical explanations are given here.

348
00:19:02,430 --> 00:19:04,710
All I will tell you is there are two kinds

349
00:19:04,710 --> 00:19:07,390
of things that people call other than Allah.

350
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:11,780
One: people call false gods, idols, mythical gods etcetera etcetera.

351
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:13,760
Angels you can even consider.

352
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:18,770
The other category is people call kings.

353
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:22,960
Besides Allah. Like who? Give us an example of a king being called besides Allah.

354
00:19:23,422 --> 00:19:27,940
Fir'own. Right? Fir'own is an example of that.
So there-- I want you to think of two entities.

355
00:19:27,950 --> 00:19:32,070
I want you to think of a giant idol that's being worshiped and I want you to think of

356
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:35,243
those who you call other than Allah.

357
00:19:37,410 --> 00:19:41,260
They cannot create a single fly. So who is incapable of creating a fly?

358
00:19:42,154 --> 00:19:47,770
Fir'own is incapable of creating a fly and the idol is incapable of creating a fly.

359
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:52,280
وَلَوِ ٱجْتَمَعُواْ لَهُۥ
even if they all got together for that purpose.

360
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:56,210
If they all, if all of your gods got
together for that purpose and Fir'own

361
00:19:56,210 --> 00:19:58,470
and all of his armies got together for that purpose.

362
00:19:58,480 --> 00:19:59,460
For what purpose?

363
00:19:59,470 --> 00:20:02,660
For the one mission of creating a single
fly,

364
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,480
they wouldn't be able to do it.

365
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:09,170
إِن يَسْلُبْهُمُ ٱلذُّبَابُ شَيْـًٔا لَّا يَسْتَنقِذُوهُ مِنْهُ

366
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:15,770
And even if, even if the fly was to
steal something away from them.

367
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:18,800
They would not be able to recover it.

368
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:22,550
They will not even be able to try to retrieve it,

369
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:25,060
they wouldn't even be able to get a piece of it back.

370
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:30,990
Now before I go to the end, which is the lesson of the example; because remember examples

371
00:20:30,990 --> 00:20:32,660
the purpose of them is to teach you a lesson.

372
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:37,770
Before I go to that I want to share something with you about this parable.

373
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:42,000
Allah 'azzawajal
is describing here

374
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:45,829
the idol and Fir'own.

375
00:20:47,140 --> 00:20:49,770
And Allah says that a fly they cannot create.

376
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:55,260
Forget creating, if a fly robbed them, they wouldn't be able to get their stuff back.

377
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:57,670
Why would He talk about a fly like that?

378
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:00,690
Well you see for many religions

379
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:05,860
with all due respect to people who you know, practice different religions,

380
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:08,450
I'm not going to make fun of a particular religion or anything like that.

381
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:11,360
But in many religions that have idol worship

382
00:21:12,290 --> 00:21:14,670
that have some kind of giant idol for whatever reason,

383
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:20,450
they don't just go and worship the idol. They put some kind of milk, honey, chocolate

384
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:21,510
Twix

385
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:22,670
Snickers

386
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,670
in front of the idol.

387
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:26,360
And then they worship.

388
00:21:27,630 --> 00:21:30,540
You know like you walk up like 4000 steps.

389
00:21:31,530 --> 00:21:35,550
And you're really thirsty, but you brought the chocolate milk for the idol.

390
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:39,550
So you put it there and you're like you're doing your thing.

391
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:41,770
Now you're a tourist

392
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,560
like from America or something.

393
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:50,370
And you go up to the the you know, 4000 steps, you're like, 'wow, that was hard.'

394
00:21:50,750 --> 00:21:51,460
'I'm thirsty.'

395
00:21:56,630 --> 00:22:01,060
If you reach for the chocolate milk that was meant for the giant idol, who's you know

396
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:05,860
that guy, what is the guy who's praying next to you or meditating, what does he do?

397
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:11,060
'Don't touch that!'

398
00:22:12,140 --> 00:22:14,060
Why? Because that's for who?

399
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:15,440
For the idol.

400
00:22:15,510 --> 00:22:19,960
The only problem with this picture is when you leave food open, unattended,

401
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:23,450
what shows up?
Flies.

402
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:29,160
So [buzzing sound] fly shows up and it sits on the nose of the idol.

403
00:22:29,840 --> 00:22:31,850
And in its fly language says,

404
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:34,460
'I'm gonna drink your chocolate milk, what you gonna do about it?'

405
00:22:36,740 --> 00:22:44,160
And then it goes down
and flies away.

406
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:45,360
Does it happen?

407
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:47,260
Sure.

408
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:53,950
And is that giant false god capable of defending its sacred food?

409
00:22:55,140 --> 00:22:59,490
These poor meditators and worshipers are constantly going, 'No, come on,

410
00:22:59,490 --> 00:23:01,460
that's for my god, leave him alone.'

411
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:03,350
Right?

412
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,290
In other words,

413
00:23:06,290 --> 00:23:10,740
this example is really powerful because Allah is saying the foundations

414
00:23:10,740 --> 00:23:17,170
of your faith are destroyed before your eyes by a small fly.

415
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:18,460
Why don't you think?

416
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:21,790
Have you ever thought about this?

417
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:25,390
You people are putting these devotions in front of your idols.

418
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:28,270
They can't even defend themselves against flies.

419
00:23:28,759 --> 00:23:30,405
وَلَوِ ٱجْتَمَعُواْ لَ

420
00:23:30,430 --> 00:23:35,090
Even if they all got together for it, 'That fly just drank chocolate milk from our god.

421
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:35,760
Let's get it.'

422
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:39,860
Like what are they gonna do?

423
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:42,050
What are they gonna do?

424
00:23:42,740 --> 00:23:47,840
But this idol was not just an idol or the people calling someone other than Allah.

425
00:23:47,840 --> 00:23:49,960
It wasn't just about idols, who else was it about?

426
00:23:50,215 --> 00:23:52,090
It's about Fir'own.

427
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:54,210
So what about Fir'own?

428
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:57,150
Fir'own is sitting up inside one of his pyramids.

429
00:23:57,940 --> 00:23:58,960
Eating a cheeseburger.

430
00:24:00,540 --> 00:24:01,770
A fly shows up.

431
00:24:04,240 --> 00:24:05,660
It takes a little bit of his lettuce.

432
00:24:07,140 --> 00:24:09,810
He finishes his bite and says, 'No one takes from Fir'own'

433
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:12,270
'Get it back.'

434
00:24:14,740 --> 00:24:18,490
So his armies are nervous. They're trying to catch this fly. They finally catch it.

435
00:24:18,670 --> 00:24:21,960
Then they're in a hurry because they quickly have to invent the microscope

436
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:23,770
and the Petri dish.

437
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:28,515
Then they have to get laser little needles to

438
00:24:28,540 --> 00:24:30,960
get the lettuce back. Can they do it?

439
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:35,360
Once it's gone,
it's gone.

440
00:24:36,040 --> 00:24:36,780
It's gone.

441
00:24:36,790 --> 00:24:38,690
I don't care how powerful Fir'own is, I don't care,

442
00:24:38,690 --> 00:24:40,200
I don't care how many armies he has.

443
00:24:40,210 --> 00:24:46,440
He is powerless when it comes to the
robbery that happened at the hands of a fly.

444
00:24:46,670 --> 00:24:51,450
If a fly was to take something away from him, he wouldn't be able to get it back.

445
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:56,150
Allah demonstrates the powerlessness of false gods and He

446
00:24:56,150 --> 00:24:58,500
doesn't need to give you some elaborate example.

447
00:24:58,510 --> 00:25:01,140
All He needs to use is a single
fly.

448
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:02,270
Subhanallah

449
00:25:03,140 --> 00:25:07,610
But this is not the lesson. This is just a preparation. The real lesson of the Ayah is

450
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:13,458
one of the most beautiful expressions in the entire Qur'an:

451
00:25:13,482 --> 00:25:15,446
